Migrated the CLI framework from manual os.Args parsing with a switch
statement to the jpillora/opts library, which provides struct-based
command definitions with automatic help generation, version info, and
argument parsing.

Each subcommand (add, del, ready) was refactored from standalone
functions accepting []string args to struct types implementing a Run()
method. The addCmd struct uses opts tags to define Title as a required
arg and Body as a variadic arg. The delCmd struct takes an ID arg. The
readyCmd struct takes no args.

The main.go was simplified from ~30 lines of manual dispatch to a
declarative config struct with opts builder calls for name, version,
summary, and repo metadata.

The README was completely rewritten from an internal format
specification (describing the TASKS.md schema, key definitions, and
locking protocol) to a user-facing document with installation
instructions, quick start examples, and concise notes about the
format, concurrency, and AI-friendliness.

An examples/TASKS.md file was added demonstrating the format with 7
sample tasks using various metadata fields (status, priority,
depends-on, assignee, component) and different statuses (closed,
inprogress, open).

Dependencies added: github.com/jpillora/opts v1.2.3 with indirect
dependencies on hashicorp/errwrap, hashicorp/go-multierror, and
posener/complete.
